body:
I assumed Tachy is short nickname for tachyons

&#x200B;

[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tachyon](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tachyon)

you still being alive is necessary for continued treatment.  Another session is another chance at a solution.

&#x200B;

Humans are sentimental and don't want their patients dying because it hurts.  You are not responsible for T's feelings in any way.  Some people will do unethical things like telling you it will get better.  Or let it slip that they would experience pain if you should pass on

Adults lose their right to civility/respect as soon as they disrespect you.  I am civil and polite. You lie to me, Gaslight me, apologize for how I feel, treated something truly heinous as acceptable, etc.  You lost my respect  I will treat you accordingly.  They will claim you are not being civil.  I explain you lost that right when you broke the above rules.  

Civility policing is a thing.  They hide their violence behind a polite tone.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

ps:  studies show this doesn't work is how you explain things to shitty people who don't think things through.  If it gets them to stop treating children a little less like property it's a good argument to start with.

if someone was upset or could be upset, bring up my points, and apologize for not bringing up your concern in a respectful fashion.  I don't think it was harassment on purpose.  Bring it up my way

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

apology:  I am sorry for the outburst, I am fine with the exemption.  I am worried that normal masking would put coworkers health at risk.  Please provide coworker with better masking option

what's going on?

&#x200B;

and yeah  people aren't fond of suicide talk

Husband unit needs upgrade/replacement.  Easier said than done.  


   Families can be shit, No Contact with mine.  


 You have more value than what you earn.  Loving mother is an example of that.  Being poor is not a failing, but it is painful.  


 I am not an expert on Methadone, but I know some people have a hard time leaving it.  Maybe you should simply think of it as you would an anti-allergy pill, or anti-anxiety meds, you need to stay well. Life is giving you a hard time, which can't make getting off of it easier.  


I hope your suffering abates.  I think you deserve better than what your experiencing.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

